cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SUCCES, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SUCCES: Stochastic Unit Commitment for Coupled European Scenarios"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "[Schoenfisch]"
    given-names: "[Theodor]"
repository-code: "https://github.com/[bellpesce]/succes"
abstract: >-
  A stochastic unit commitment and economic dispatch simulator for 15
  European power market regions. Dispatch is optimised by a real-valued
  island genetic algorithm with block crossover, evaluated against
  CVaR-weighted scenario banks with stochastic demand, renewable output,
  hydro inflow and forced outages. Regions are coupled via PTDF-based ATC
  flows. Pricing is pure merit order: the last dispatched unit sets the
  market clearing price. No MILP/LP solver is used anywhere.
keywords:
  - unit commitment
  - economic dispatch
  - genetic algorithm
  - power markets
  - stochastic optimization
  - electricity prices
  - Julia
  - Python
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-10"
